<h2>FAQ: Moving to Spain</h2>
<p>Do I need to speak Spanish to move to Spain?</p>
<p>No, but it helps. Major cities have English speakers. Learning basics (15-20 mins/day for 3 months) is helpful. Most English speakers manage fine, especially initially.</p>
<p>How much money do I need to move?</p>
<p>Startup costs: €3,500-8,000. Monthly living: €1,500-2,500. Save €10,000-15,000 to move comfortably with a cushion.</p>
<p>Can I bring my car from my home country?</p>
<p>Yes. Vehicle registration changes to Spanish plates (process takes 2-4 weeks). You&#x27;ll need Spanish insurance and emissions inspection. Total cost: €500-1,500.</p>
<p>What if my visa is denied?</p>
<p>You can appeal (4-8 weeks) or reapply with stronger documentation. Don&#x27;t panic; most denials are fixable. Consult a specialist if unsure.</p>
